{ Now let us fix and restrict a weak pawn: a backward pawn cannot advance safely, and no other pawn can defend it. Push to e5 so his stays stuck forever. [%cal Ye4e5] } 1. e5 { The d6 pawn cannot escape to d5. Your pawn joins the attack without trading a rook for it. [%tail] [%cal Ge4e5] } (1. Rxd6 { Your rook spends itself on a single pawn, before you have even added the extra attacker. } 1... Bxd6 2. Bxd6 2... Rxd6 { You gave a rook and a bishop for his bishop and one pawn, and his rook on d6 is safe. Push to e5 first. [%csl Rd6] }) 1... Qc6 2. h3 2... Kf8 3. Bg3 3... Qe4 4. exd6 { The backward pawn finally falls, yours for nothing in return. [%cal Ge5d6] } 1-0


[Event "Lasker plans: Fix the target before aiming at it"]
[Site "https://lichess.org/analysis/r1bq1rk1/1p3ppp/p1nbpn2/3p4/1PP5/P1N1PN2/1B3PPP/R2QKB1R_w_KQ_-_0_10"]
