{ His bishop wants a diagonal. Can you keep the doubled c pawns from opening one? } 20. c4 { You stop the c5 pawn from advancing. The c6 pawn cannot follow it and free the bishop. [%tail] [%cal Gc2c4] } (20. e4 { You strike in the middle instead. It opens lines — including one for the bishop you are trying to bury. } 20... c4 21. dxc4 { You use the d pawn to make room on its file. The b pawn can recapture too. } 21... dxe4 22. Qxe4 { The middle opens and both sides get play. Freezing his pawns is the gain that can never be undone. [%cal Gc2c4] }) (20. Bb2 { The bishop takes the long diagonal, flexible and fine. Meanwhile his pawn on c5 can still march and let his own bishop out. [%cal Bb2h8] } 20... c4 21. dxc4 { There it goes: the pawn advances and his bishop can breathe again. [%cal Gc2c4] }) (20. Nd2 { The knight looks for a better square. His c pawns are still free to move, and they are what keeps his bishop shut in. } 20... Bb7 { Your knight is better placed, and his position is looser than it needed to be. [%cal Gc2c4] }) (20. Kf1 { A safe king move with nothing to answer. It is the pawns that decide this position. } 20... Bb7 { Safe — and he is one pawn push away from freeing the piece you wanted buried. [%cal Gc2c4] }) (20. Kf2 { Another quiet king step. It changes nothing that his bishop cares about. } 20... f6 { Still safe, still nothing collected. A pawn on c4 settles that bishop for the rest of the game. [%cal Gc2c4] }) (20. Kg2 { The king tucks into the corner. Comfortable — and his bishop on a8 is only waiting for c5 to advance. } 20... c4 21. dxc4 { And he plays it. The pawn to c4 was the one move that could have stopped it for ever. [%cal Gc2c4] }) (20. h4 { Space on the far wing, where neither his bishop nor his king has any interest. } 20... c4 21. dxc4 { He frees his bishop at once, and a little space on the edge does not make up for it. [%cal Gc2c4] }) 20... f6 21. Bb2 { Your bishop steps aside, and the frozen pawns still keep his own bishop shut in on a8. [%cal Gc1b2] } 1-0


[Event "Lasker plans: Trade the fianchetto defender"]
[Site "https://lichess.org/analysis/r2q1rk1/pbp1npbp/1pnpp1p1/4P3/3P4/2NBBN2/PPPQ1PPP/R4RK1_w_-_-_0_2"]
