{ His f pawn has moved. Can you remove the defender before organizing pressure on e6? } 13. Bxe7 { You remove his bishop, then prepare to bring the rooks to the e column. [%cal Gg5e7] } (13. Be3 { The bishop steps back, solid enough. His bishop stays on e7, standing in the e column right in front of the pawn you want to attack. } 13... Qd5 { A useful move for him, and his bishop is still shielding the backward pawn behind it. [%cal Gg5e7] }) (13. Bf4 { The bishop takes a natural square. It is the trade on e7 that clears the column in front of his weak pawn. } 13... Nf6 { He develops, and the shield on e7 is still standing. [%cal Gg5e7] }) 13... Qxe7 { His queen has to take over the bishop job. } 14. O-O { Your king is safe, and the rook on f1 is one step away from the column you cleared. [%tail] [%cal Ge1g1] } (14. Bc2 { The bishop tucks safely onto c2. Strong too — but castling puts a rook on the column you have just cleared. } 14... Qg5 { A fair try from him. Castling gets the king safe and a rook to e1 in the same breath. [%cal Ge1g1] }) (14. O-O-O { Castling the other way is sound as well. It sends the rook to d1, and the column you cleared is the e one. } 14... c5 { Both castles are playable. This one leaves the rook that wants e1 sitting in the corner. [%cal Ge1g1] }) (14. f4 { The pawn props up your knight on e5. Useful — and your king is still in the middle with two rooks out of touch. } 14... a5 { He gets on with his own play while your rooks are still strangers. Castling introduces them. [%cal Ge1g1] }) (14. g4 { A pawn lunge on the wing with your king still standing in the center. } 14... c5 15. dxc5 15... Qxc5 { He has time to reorganize, and your rook has still not found the e column. [%cal Ge1g1] }) (14. Qe3 { The queen takes the e column herself. She is a heavy first attacker; the rook is the piece that belongs there. } 14... Nc7 { A fair try. Castle, and the rook reaches e1 with your king already safe. [%cal Ge1g1] }) 14... c5 15. Rfe1 { Your rook lands on the e column, adding real pressure next to your knight. [%cal Gf1e1] } 1-0


[Event "Lasker plans: Avoid helping the enemy pawn advance"]
[Site "https://lichess.org/analysis/rnbqk2r/ppp1bppp/4p3/3p2B1/2PPn3/2N1P3/PP3PPP/R2QKBNR_w_KQkq_-_0_6"]
